-- title:
--   Realising Tₚ in the corner Hecke ring with residual trace
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $k$ factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $0$ and the whole space. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p \in S$, and $N \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N$ and all prime divisors of $N$ in $S$. Let $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and satisfy: for primes $q \neq p$, $q \in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some element of some inertia subgroup at $q$ acts non-trivially); every $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ divides $N$; a prime $q \neq p$ dividing $N$ but not in $S_{\min}$ satisfies $q^2 \mid N$; $q^3 \nmid N$ for all primes $q \neq p$; and for $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on $\bar\rho$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ have an integral structure (the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is everything), and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ acting as $x \mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^1 =$ `H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`, the additive maps from $\Gamma_0(N)$ to $\mathcal{O}$; let $Sp$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$ exhausting the maximal ideals and $e_j \in \mathfrak{m}_{j'}$ iff $j \neq j'$) and $i$ an index, with corner $C = e_i \cdot H^1$ finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Let $t$ and $c$ assign to each generator $g$ (a symbol $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid N$; $U_q$ with $q$ prime dividing $N$; or a diamond $\langle d \rangle$, $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$) an element $t_g \in \mathbb{T}$ and a scalar $c_g \in \mathcal{O}$, subject to: every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91); $t_g$ acts as the operator attached to $g$; $t_g - c_g \in \mathfrak{m}_i$; the corner is cofull, that is, any $v \in H^1$ such that for all $g$ and all $k$ some power $(t_g - c_g)^n$ sends $v$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k H^1$ already lies in $C$; the residue of $c_{T_\ell}$ is $\theta(T_\ell)$; $c_{U_q} \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ whenever $q \neq p$, $q \mid N$ and $q^2 \mid N$; and $c_{\langle d\rangle} \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$. Assume finally $C \neq 0$ and that the corner ring `Sp.CornerRing i` acts faithfully on $C$. Then there is an element $t_p$ of the corner ring such that, first, $t_p \cdot m = T_p m$ in $H^1$ for every $m \in C$, where $T_p$ is the transfer operator `heckeT N ⊤ p 𝒪`; and second, for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $p$ for $P$, every endomorphism $E$ of the inertia coinvariants $\bar\rho.V / \sum_{\tau \in I_P} \mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$, and every $a \in \mathcal{O}$ whose residue is $\mathrm{tr}\,E$, one has for each $m \in C$ and each $k$ some $n$ with $(t_p - a)^n \cdot m \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k H^1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Hecke operator at the residue characteristic $p$ — which is not among the generators of the anemic Hecke algebra, since $p \in S$ — is nevertheless realised by an element of the local corner Hecke ring acting on $e_i H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal{O})$, and that this element is congruent, in the topological sense stated, to the trace of Frobenius on the inertia coinvariants of $\bar\rho$ at $p$. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_and_apply_eq_trace_of_subfamily_point`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_and_apply_eq_trace_of_subfamily_point), which packages the operator together with its residual value for the subfamily-based corner data.
